Subject: [PATCH 2/2] notmuch: Keep messages tagged archive out of the inbox
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Change-Id: vuzokylmyzpytntsuutntltwvkkmvruk

The archive tag marks a message the user has asked to archive but whose
file just archive has not yet moved. mail-tag.sh derives inbox from the
maildir alone, so every notmuch new until the move put such a message
back in the inbox, undoing the "a" key in notmuch-emacs.

inbox should never sit beside sent, replied or archive. Honoring the
request keeps it that way, and the request costs nothing if lost: a
rebuilt database brings the message back to the inbox, as it should for
a message that was never moved.
---
change-id: vuzokylmyzpytntsuutntltwvkkmvruk

 dotfiles/notmuch/hooks/mail-tag.sh | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dotfiles/notmuch/hooks/mail-tag.sh b/dotfiles/notmuch/hooks/mail-tag.sh
index 269caaf..aced0fe 100755
--- a/dotfiles/notmuch/hooks/mail-tag.sh
+++ b/dotfiles/notmuch/hooks/mail-tag.sh
@@ -7,12 +7,18 @@
 # the maildir and the same tags come back.
 #
 #   sent     from the user (notmuch user.primary_email or other_email)
-#   inbox    from someone else, and the user has not replied to it
+#   inbox    from someone else, not replied to and not tagged archive
 #   replied  from someone else, and the user has replied to it
 #
 # "Replied to" means a message from the user names it in In-Reply-To.
 # Drafts get none of these tags.
 #
+# The archive tag is the one input that lives only in the database: a
+# request, set by "a" in notmuch-emacs, for just archive to move the
+# message under archive/. It keeps the message out of the inbox until
+# then. If the database is rebuilt first, the request is lost and the
+# message is back in the inbox, which is right, since it never moved.
+#
 # Runs from the notmuch post-new hook, so notmuch new applies it.
 
 set -eu
@@ -28,6 +34,7 @@ main() {
 		echo "-sent -inbox -replied -- ${drafts}"
 		echo "+sent -inbox -replied -- (${me}) and not ${drafts}"
 		echo "-sent +inbox -replied -- not (${me}) and not ${drafts}"
+		echo "-inbox -- tag:archive"
 		replied_ids "${me}" | while read -r id; do
 			echo "+replied -inbox -- id:\"${id}\" and not (${me}) and not ${drafts}"
 		done
